---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LesionRule from '../components/ornament/LesionRule.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../consts';

/**
 * Winnow's page while Winnow has nowhere to live.
 *
 * Deliberately short. The long account is the Appendix entry in the projects
 * collection; this is the page a nav button needs to point at, and until the
 * thing is running the most useful page is one that says what it does, what
 * it was measured at, and why it is not open yet.
 */

/** Every figure written as a budget first, then measured on 100,000 records. */
const BUDGETS = [
  ['Screening, 95th percentile', '32–69 ms', '80 ms'],
  ['Record list, across 15 filters, sorts and searches', '12–64 ms', '150 ms'],
  ['Import of 100,000 records', '49 s', '60 s'],
  ['Deduplication of 50,000 records', '13 s', '30 s'],
  ['Page load on 4G (LCP)', '0.7 s', '1.5 s'],
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title={`Winnow — a platform for systematic reviews — ${AUTHOR}`}
  description="Free, open-source and self-hostable: search results in, PRISMA 2020 diagram out, on a server the lab owns."
  folio="—"
>
  <div class="codex wn">
    <p class="wn-kicker" data-reveal>Built · awaiting a server</p>
    <h1 class="wn-h1" data-press>Winnow</h1>
    <p class="wn-lede codex-measure" data-reveal>
      Separate the evidence from the noise. A systematic review starts with
      thousands of database records and ends with a diagram every reader
      expects; the tools that carry it between the two are commercial and
      closed, and they want your unpublished data on their servers. Winnow is
      the whole pipeline instead — free, open source, and running on a machine
      the lab owns.
    </p>

    <LesionRule />

    <section class="wn-sec" aria-labelledby="wn-what">
      <h2 class="wn-h2" id="wn-what">What it does</h2>
      <ul class="wn-list codex-measure" data-reveal-stagger>
        <li>Twenty search exports at once — RIS, PubMed MEDLINE and XML, BibTeX, EndNote XML, Zotero RDF, CSV — with live progress and undo.</li>
        <li>Deduplication that merges the certain pairs and puts the doubtful ones side by side for a person.</li>
        <li>Keyboard-first screening, blind or open, two reviewers, with conflicts resolved against each other's reasons.</li>
        <li>A relevance model that retrains from each reviewer's own decisions, shows the likely includes first, and estimates when stopping is defensible.</li>
        <li>Full texts uploaded or fetched from Unpaywall and PubMed Central, virus-scanned before anyone opens them.</li>
        <li>Dual data extraction on versioned forms with a consensus step, and risk of bias in RoB 2, ROBINS-I, Newcastle–Ottawa or QUADAS-2.</li>
        <li>Out the other end: the PRISMA 2020 flow diagram, Cohen's and Fleiss' kappa, a methods paragraph to paste, and a backup that restores anywhere.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="wn-sec" aria-labelledby="wn-fast">
      <h2 class="wn-h2" id="wn-fast">How well it works</h2>
      <p class="wn-note codex-measure" data-reveal>
        Every number below was written down as a budget before it was
        measured, and measured on reviews of 100,000 records.
      </p>
      <table class="wn-table" data-reveal>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">What</th><th scope="col">Measured</th><th scope="col">Budget</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {BUDGETS.map(([what, measured, budget]) => (
            <tr><th scope="row">{what}</th><td>{measured}</td><td>{budget}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="wn-note codex-measure" data-reveal>
        Fifty reviewers deciding every three seconds for ten minutes: a 37 ms
        95th percentile and 0 errors in 19,920 requests. Authorisation is
        checked per review with PostgreSQL row-level security behind it, and
        blind mode is enforced in the database rather than hidden in the
        interface. WCAG 2.2 AA with no serious or critical axe findings across
        43 pages, four screen sizes and both themes. 900 backend tests at 95%
        coverage, Playwright end to end, <code>mypy --strict</code>, and an
        OWASP ZAP baseline scan in CI with no high-risk findings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="wn-sec" aria-labelledby="wn-live">
      <h2 class="wn-h2" id="wn-live">Not live yet</h2>
      <p class="wn-note codex-measure" data-reveal>
        The production stack is complete and tested — one command brings it up
        with automatic HTTPS, encrypted nightly backups and a restore test CI
        runs monthly. What it does not have is somewhere to run. Winnow keeps
        its own database, a background worker and a virus scanner, so it needs
        a paid server rather than the free static hosting the rest of this site
        uses. It goes up at <strong>winnow.sandhiresearch.org</strong> for
        Sandhi Research Lab once that server is in place, and this page becomes
        a link on the day it does.
      </p>
      <p class="wn-actions" data-reveal>
        <a class="wn-btn" href="https://github.com/asifuddin01/WINNOW">Read the source</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wn { padding-top: clamp(2.4rem, 9vh, 5rem); }
  .wn-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brass-text);
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .wn-h1 { font-size: var(--t-2xl); margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .wn-lede { font-size: var(--body-size); line-height: var(--body-leading); }

  .wn-sec { margin-top: 2.6rem; }
  .wn-h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .wn-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  .wn-list li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .wn-note { line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 1rem; }

  .wn-table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
  }
  .wn-table th,
  .wn-table td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem 0.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: var(--rule) solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 28%, transparent);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .wn-table thead th {
    color: var(--brass-text);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-bottom-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 55%, transparent);
  }
  .wn-table tbody th { color: var(--ink); }
  .wn-table td { color: var(--ink-soft); white-space: nowrap; }

  .wn-actions { margin: 1.2rem 0 0; }
  .wn-btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: var(--rule) solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 55%, transparent);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
  }
  .wn-btn:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brass) 14%, transparent); }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .wn-table { font-size: 0.75rem; }
    .wn-table th, .wn-table td { padding-right: 0.5rem; }
  }
</style>
